00001| /* ============================================================================
00002|    qalarc · OSINT Hub — LITE cloud API (Cloudflare Pages Function)
00003|    Route file: functions/api/[[path]].js  →  serves same-origin /api/*
00004| 
00005|    WHY THIS EXISTS
00006|    ---------------
00007|    The full engine is a FastAPI backend running maigret / holehe / phoneinfoga
00008|    as local subprocesses — impossible on Pages. This Function provides a
00009|    zero-server subset ("lite") so the deployed static frontend stays useful:
00010| 
00011|      GET  /api/health      → lite health marker (mode:"lite")
00012|      GET  /api/tools       → the two lite tools
00013|      POST /api/lite/check  → synchronous edge username scan (~44 platforms)
00014|      POST /api/lite/pivots → instant Google-dork pivots for a phone number
00015|      *    /api/*           → 501 (full engine not available in lite mode)
00016| 
00017|    FREE-PLAN SUBREQUEST BUDGET (the design constraint)
00018|    --------------------------------------------------
00019|    Workers/Pages Functions on the Cloudflare FREE plan allow **50 subrequests
00020|    per incoming request**. Every external fetch() counts as one subrequest —
00021|    and a redirect chain counts once PER HOP. Therefore:
00022| 
00023|      • every probe uses redirect:"manual" → exactly ONE subrequest per site,
00024|        no matter how the target would redirect;
00025|      • the site list is hard-capped at 44 entries (44 < 50, leaving headroom);
00026|      • probes run in chunks of 10 concurrent fetches (Promise.allSettled) to
00027|        stay polite and inside CPU limits (free plan: 10 ms CPU/request —
00028|        awaiting fetches does not consume CPU);
00029|      • each fetch is bounded by AbortSignal.timeout(8000) so a hanging host
00030|        cannot stall the whole request;
00031|      • no redirect is followed, so per-site detection works from the immediate
00032|        status code + Location header (see SITES below).
00033| 
00034|    DETECTION RULES (conservative by design — verified empirically 2026-09)
00035|    -----------------------------------------------------------------------
00036|    Sites were probed with a known-existing and a known-missing username:
00037|    only platforms whose missing-profile response is reliably distinguishable
00038|    are included. Unreliable platforms that answer HTTP 200 for *any* username
00039|    (instagram, tiktok, twitch, spotify, pinterest, kaggle, pypi, mixcloud,
00040|    imgur, dailymotion, artstation, 500px, slideshare …) are deliberately
00041|    OMITTED — a false "found" is worse than a missing row.
00042|    Rule kinds (per site):
00043|      status    (default) found ⇔ 2xx            (missing ⇒ 404/403/redirect)
00044|      redirUser             found ⇔ 2xx, or 3xx whose Location still contains
00045|                            the username (canonicalisation redirect; missing is
00046|                            a plain 404 on these sites)
00047|      roblox                special: 3xx whose Location is NOT the
00048|                            "request-error" page (missing users bounce there)
00049|      sniff                 2xx AND cheap body markers (tiny JSON pages or the
00050|                            steam error string; body reads skipped if huge)
00051| 
00052|    No state, no KV, no analytics. A best-effort in-memory per-IP rate limiter
00053|    (30/hour) lives only for the isolate's lifetime — best effort, not a
00054|    guarantee. Plain JS, no build step, no external packages.
00055| ============================================================================ */
00056| 
